+# Changes
+
+## Round 0
+
+First pass; no REVIEW.md findings to address yet.
+
+- `src/truncate.mjs` (new): exports `truncate(text, max)`. Returns `text`
+  unchanged when `text.length <= max`; otherwise returns the first `max - 1`
+  characters followed by "…" (U+2026), so the result is exactly `max` long.
+  A non-string `text` throws `TypeError`; a `max` that is not a positive
+  integer (`0`, `-1`, `2.5`, `"3"`, `NaN`, `Infinity`, `undefined`) throws
+  `RangeError`. Same shape and messages as `src/pad.mjs`.
+- `tests/truncate.test.mjs` (new): covers short text, the boundary at exactly
+  `max`, cutting with the ellipsis and exact length, `max` of 1 (returns "…"),
+  whitespace at the cut (kept, not trimmed, so the length stays exactly `max`),
+  and the refused `text` and `max` values.
+- `CHANGELOG.md`: added a `truncate` line under `## Unreleased` in the style of
+  the `padStart` entry.
+
+Decisions on points the task leaves open: "characters" means UTF-16 code
+units (`.length`), matching `padStart`; whitespace before the cut is kept
+rather than trimmed, since trimming would break the exact-`max` length rule.
